  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1010 PM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nUL high will continue to sit over the Four Corners for Tuesday,\nwhich will continue to limit precip across the area. With that\nsaid, we will be a little hotter tomorrow with a little bit more\nmoisture. Although most locations will remain dry and our best \nstorm chances will be over the Gila, the HRRR and the NAM Nest do \nshow a bit more storm coverage over the lowlands, especially west \nof the Continental Divide. I'm not sure I buy the eastward extent \nof the HRRR, which brings storms as far east as El Paso, but I \ndid pull up POPs toward the Luna / Dona Ana County line.\n\nWe're still on track for a pattern change for Wednesday. The Four\nCorners high will shift toward the Southern Plains and Gulf Coast,\nbringing in southerly flow for New Mexico and Far West Texas. The\nGFS also continues to hint at the passage of a weak wave Wednesday\nnight into Thursday. Either way, this pattern will persist into \nthe weekend with rain and storm chances covering most of the area.\nAfter that, the UL high will start making a westward shift, but \nhow far west is yet to be seen. The GFS and Euro also show an \neastward wave moving through Northern Mexico Sunday, but its\ninfluence may only reach as far north as the International Border.",
